    "## Predicting Customer Churn in a Digital Banking Environment\n",
    "\n",
    "### Introduction\n",
    "Digital banks, in particular, face increasing challenges from innovative fintech startups and rapidly evolving customer expectations. In this project, we aim to address the issue of customer churn for a digital bank that has been experiencing fluctuating retention rates. To do this, we focus on helping the bank improve its retention efforts by using different machine learning techniques.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Objectives\n",
    "The primary objective of this project is to develop predictive models capable of accurately identifying customers at high risk of churn. Specifically, we aim to:\n",
    "\n",
    "- Analyze and understand key features contributing to customer churn.\n",
    "- Apply machine learning algorithms to classify customers based on their churn risk.\n",
    "- Provide actionable insights that the bank can use to reduce churn and improve customer engagement.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Machine Learning Models\n",
    "To address the classification problem, we will apply and compare the performance of the following machine learning algorithms:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)**  \n",
    "   A non-parametric method that classifies a data point based on how its neighbors are classified.\n",
    "\n",
    "2. **Logistic Regression**  \n",
    "   A statistical model that uses a logistic function to model a binary dependent variable, particularly useful for understanding the influence of predictor variables on churn probability.\n",
    "\n",
    "3. **Support Vector Machines (SVM)**  \n",
    "   A supervised learning model that seeks to find the optimal hyperplane to separate data into two classes, useful for high-dimensional feature spaces.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Dataset Description\n",
    "We’re working with a dataset containing 1,000 customer records, each with several features describing their financial health and digital behavior. The customers are labeled as either high or low risk of churn based on business-defined rules.\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Financial Health Indicators\n",
    "- `account_balance`: Total account balance  \n",
    "- `monthly_income`: Estimated monthly income  \n",
    "- `num_transactions`: Number of recent financial transactions  \n",
    "- `credit_score`: Creditworthiness of the customer  \n",
    "\n",
    "#### Digital Behavior Metrics\n",
    "- `login_frequency`: Frequency of user logins  \n",
    "- `mobile_app_usage`: Number of interactions with the mobile application  \n",
    "- `customer_support_calls`: Number of times the customer contacted support  \n",
    "- `avg_session_time`: Average duration of user sessions  \n",
    "\n",
    "#### Target Variable\n",
    "- `churn_risk` (Binary classification):  \n",
    "  - `1` = High churn risk (650 customers)  \n",
    "  - `0` = Low churn risk (350 customers)  \n",
