    "## kNN\n",
    "In this study, we applied the k-Nearest Neighbors (kNN) algorithm to classify data based on selected features from our dataset. kNN is a supervised machine learning algorithm that classifies new data points by considering the majority class among its nearest neighbors in the training set. \n",
    "\n",
    "We used the k-Nearest Neighbors (kNN) algorithm to classify data by finding the optimal number of neighbors (K) that gives the best accuracy. First, we start by re-splitting the dataset using the best-performing test size and random state identified earlier, then we selected the top 10 features using Random Forest and Recursive Feature Elimination. Then, we trained kNN models across different K values and evaluated their training and test accuracies. The goal was to identify the best K that provides the highest test accuracy, which we visualized using a plot. \n"
   ]
